{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (DOCTOR): Come, sit. What has been going on with this young man?",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Doctor, this is Rohan, he is five. Fever and cough, it is two days now, from Tuesday.",
  "[SEG0003] person_3 (CAREGIVER): Two days? Ma'am, Sunday evening itself he was warm. I was giving him a bath, I remember. Today is Thursday, so four days, no?",
  "[SEG0004] person_2 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Sunday he was only a little dull. The proper fever, um, I thought Monday, no, it was Tuesday night. I am sure.",
  "[SEG0005] person_1 (DOCTOR): Okay. So we are somewhere between two and four days, and that is not settled. Rohan beta, how are you feeling?",
  "[SEG0006] person_4 (PATIENT): Bad.",
  "[SEG0007] person_1 (DOCTOR): Oh, bad. What is bothering you, the cough?",
  "[SEG0008] person_4 (PATIENT): Cough.",
  "[SEG0009] person_2 (FAMILY_MEMBER): At night it gets worse, doctor. Dry cough, and then he does not sleep. I was awake till two o'clock.",
  "[SEG0010] person_3 (CAREGIVER): And the fever, last night the thermometer showed one hundred and three. I even wrote it on the calendar.",
  "[SEG0011] person_2 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Aunty, please. I saw one hundred point four, not one hundred and three. That thermometer beeps whenever it feels like.",
  "[SEG0012] person_1 (DOCTOR): Home numbers love to argue. Any running nose, or is the breathing hard for him?",
  "[SEG0013] person_2 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Little running nose, yes. Breathing is okay. No wheezing, nothing of that sort.",
  "[SEG0014] person_1 (DOCTOR): Rohan, tell me, does your tummy hurt?",
  "[SEG0015] person_4 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0016] person_2 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Morning he was holding his stomach, doctor, and he said it is paining. He left the cartoon and all.",
  "[SEG0017] person_4 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0018] person_1 (DOCTOR): Alright, beta, I am listening. What about water and food at home?",
  "[SEG0019] person_3 (CAREGIVER): Water he takes. Food, only two spoons of rice and some curd. We did give syrup for the fever.",
  "[SEG0020] person_1 (DOCTOR): Which syrup, and how much went into the spoon?",
  "[SEG0021] person_2 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Crocin, the paracetamol, pink syrup. One spoon, five ml, three times yesterday, for the fever.",
  "[SEG0022] person_3 (CAREGIVER): This morning I gave Brufen, the ibuprofen. Half a spoon. I thought the Crocin was finished, so I used the other bottle.",
  "[SEG0023] person_2 (FAMILY_MEMBER): No, no, Brufen is Diya's, my elder girl. For Rohan I opened a new Crocin. You gave half a spoon of that only, not Brufen. The bottle was on the table.",
  "[SEG0024] person_3 (CAREGIVER): Half? The marking is all faded, ma'am. Maybe it was a full spoon. I cannot swear now.",
  "[SEG0025] person_1 (DOCTOR): So for Rohan it was paracetamol, not the ibuprofen, but the spoon is not a number I can trust. Any medicine allergy?",
  "[SEG0026] person_2 (FAMILY_MEMBER): No, nothing. He has had Crocin before, no rash, no problem.",
  "[SEG0027] person_1 (DOCTOR): Any asthma, any operation, anything that keeps coming back?",
  "[SEG0028] person_3 (CAREGIVER): No asthma, no operation. Last year loose motions for two days, then he was fine. He goes to LKG at St Mary's, the one near the market.",
  "[SEG0029] person_2 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Aunty stays with us, she manages him when I am at the bank. The parking downstairs was completely mad, we nearly... anyway, sorry.",
  "[SEG0030] person_1 (DOCTOR): Let me look at him. Open your mouth, good boy. Throat is a little red. Ears are fine. Chest is clear, no crackles that I can hear.",
  "[SEG0031] person_1 (DOCTOR): Just now the temperature is thirty seven point four, and the pulse is one hundred and ten. He is warm, but he looks comfortable.",
  "[SEG0032] person_2 (FAMILY_MEMBER): So you are saying it is not pneumonia?",
  "[SEG0033] person_1 (DOCTOR): My working impression is a viral cough and cold. The chest is clear, so I am not calling it a chest infection today.",
  "[SEG0034] person_1 (DOCTOR): Continue the paracetamol syrup, five ml, that is a proper spoon, up to four times a day only if the fever is there. Plenty of fluids, and let him rest from school tomorrow.",
  "[SEG0035] person_1 (DOCTOR): If the cough does not settle, we might do a chest x-ray. Not something for today.",
  "[SEG0036] person_2 (FAMILY_MEMBER): When do we show him again?",
  "[SEG0037] person_1 (DOCTOR): Let's see him in one week. If he is breathing fast, or you cannot wake him properly, do not wait for that, just come."
 ],
